{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-fourier-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-fourier-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the categorical Fourier transform","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-laplace-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-fourier-exists"],"tags":["existence","fourier","peter-weyl"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalFourier.exists","text":"categorical-fourier-transform-exists.md","leanSource":"categorical-fourier-transform-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-fourier-exists\"></a><p>For the ground ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R_q = \\mathbb{Z}[q, q^{-1}]</code>, the Peter–Weyl decomposition of the quantum observable universe yields a categorical Fourier transform <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{F}</code>: a monoidal functor intertwining the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-convolution with the pointwise product on irreducible components,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{F}(f \\ast_q g) = \\mathcal{F}(f) \\cdot \\mathcal{F}(g).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.21.15","page":"b/prop-categorical-fourier-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":70},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalFourier.exists","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-univer